WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:01.497
Warning! Warning!

2
00:00:01.497 --> 00:00:06.705
I built this with AI and text to speech, because I can't narrate for shit!

3
00:00:08.100 --> 00:00:11.126
Voyage put out an update on the seventeenth of November.

4
00:00:11.126 --> 00:00:14.908
I went through it in a brand new blank world and in my Workshop world.

5
00:00:14.908 --> 00:00:17.070
Three things matter if you build worlds.

6
00:00:18.467 --> 00:00:20.165
First, NPC intents.

7
00:00:20.165 --> 00:00:24.543
This is a brand new world, made after the update.

8
00:00:24.543 --> 00:00:30.977
Under Characters, NPCs, NPC Settings, always run NPC intents starts off.

9
00:00:31.433 --> 00:00:34.294
Here's my Workshop world, made before the update.

10
00:00:34.294 --> 00:00:40.073
Studio shows it off here too, because nothing's saved yet, but Voyage says older worlds keep it on.

11
00:00:40.073 --> 00:00:43.984
If your world needs it, switch it on yourself and there's no doubt.

12
00:00:44.433 --> 00:00:48.078
When it's off, NPCs only plan their own moves on combat turns.

13
00:00:48.078 --> 00:00:51.723
The rest of the time, the narrator alone decides what they do.

14
00:00:51.723 --> 00:00:56.602
So if your NPC intents instructions do real work, switch it on before anyone plays.

15
00:00:56.602 --> 00:00:59.306
A game that's already running can't change it.

16
00:01:00.700 --> 00:01:03.819
Second, you can write your own opening now.

17
00:01:03.819 --> 00:01:07.445
Open a story start under Game Start, Story Starts.

18
00:01:07.900 --> 00:01:10.719
There's a new box called authored opening.

19
00:01:10.719 --> 00:01:16.758
It's shown exactly as written, with no AI rewriting, so write it for solo and multiplayer.

20
00:01:17.200 --> 00:01:20.466
Once there's text in it, you can add scene NPCs.

21
00:01:20.466 --> 00:01:24.003
They're in the scene, but they don't join the party.

22
00:01:24.467 --> 00:01:28.072
You can set the day, the time of day and the music too,

23
00:01:28.072 --> 00:01:31.874
and the music has to be a playlist your world already has.

24
00:01:32.333 --> 00:01:35.794
Fallback says what happens when the opening can't be used.

25
00:01:35.794 --> 00:01:40.270
Generate writes one instead, and error reports it so you can fix the start.

26
00:01:40.733 --> 00:01:44.881
It needs at least one starting location, or Studio flags it.

27
00:01:44.881 --> 00:01:51.310
And the text doesn't give anything, so starting items and quests still go in their own boxes.

28
00:01:52.700 --> 00:01:53.700
Third, skills.

29
00:01:53.700 --> 00:01:57.746
A trigger can now give a skill the character doesn't have yet.

30
00:01:57.746 --> 00:01:59.769
Before the update, it couldn't.

31
00:01:59.769 --> 00:02:05.120
A trait that boosts a skill the character doesn't have now creates that skill too.

32
00:02:05.120 --> 00:02:08.775
If you built a workaround for this, it's worth a retest.

33
00:02:10.167 --> 00:02:11.379
The rest is quick.

34
00:02:11.379 --> 00:02:15.216
Image links on Voyage's own hosts can be short paths now,

35
00:02:15.216 --> 00:02:19.458
and they no longer count against your world's character limits.

36
00:02:19.458 --> 00:02:23.969
Renamed skills, resources, locations and areas keep their progress.

37
00:02:23.969 --> 00:02:29.355
With PvP damage off, players can't hurt, control or rob each other's characters.

38
00:02:29.355 --> 00:02:36.222
And republish your world if you want NPC alternate portraits ready ahead of time in visual novel mode.

39
00:02:37.633 --> 00:02:42.335
That's it. My worlds and lorebooks are at deaththegrim.github.io.

40
00:02:42.800 --> 00:02:46.748
I'm Dreamer. Now go build something weird, and I'll see you next time!

